  "scoreInterpretation": "Comparative against the independently inspected original and fixed target, using the frozen Ellis outcomes. These are observations, not universal numerical pass thresholds.",
  "observations": [
    "The native reconstruction visibly improves the source toward the fixed warm soft target. The cap crown has padded curvature, a coherent folded front band/brim and restrained panel lines; the head/ears, palms and cuffs have gentle volume instead of the source hard planar transitions. The new construction is useful native design work, not a reason to demand the original part counts or slab shapes.",
    "Ellis remains recognizable in all facings: light golden skin, ginger curls, round dark glasses, blue/navy cap, ivory coat, orange apron/tie and dark shoes. The front face remains friendly and readable at logical192x320. Ginger hair, skin and apron remain separate through shape and value despite their warm palette family.",
    "Cap highlights are broad and soft, the coat is ivory with clean cuff/collar transitions, and the apron has readable straps, fastenings, pocket edging and hem structure. The previous harsh faceted side sleeves are substantially improved. Hair masses have softer transitions and less rigid pellet-grid repetition, including an intentional back silhouette and back coat/tie detail.",
    "All192 indexed frames were inspected at logical size on light, neutral gray and dark backgrounds through48 pixel-verified contact sheets. No material alpha fringe, detached speck, blown highlight, crushed cap/hair dead spot, flickering seam, or new cap/fringe/glasses/sleeve defect was found. E/W profile details and all work/hold/load frames remain coherent.",
    "The actual native knife has separate wood-colored handle and pale steel-colored blade meshes/materials. Its grip follows the original right palm; the blade stays distinct in the work profiles. The handle is largely occluded by the authored grip, which is consistent with the source rather than missing geometry.",
    "All16 bound MP4s were played in the supplied browser index at logical size and independently decoded: each has twelve384x640 frames at12fps and one-second duration. Idle/work/hold continued looping; all four load previews completed and stopped with the dish still held. Source-like subtle idle bob, work tilt/hand motion and out-and-back load were retained, without visible garment or attachment popping.",
    "Twelve loop boundary previews and actual key13 native captures were inspected. Direct pixel checks find at most1/255 channel differences in8..19 pixels per frame; independent native bone and visible-prop closure errors are exactly zero. There is no visible loop jump, and the thirteenth closure key is correctly excluded from the atlases.",
    "All17 native context images were inspected: declared serving-belt/customer placements, additional fixed belt-dish context and90-degree side contexts. Body scale and clearance remain coherent. The front belt rail obscures much of the authored work pose as it did in the source; side contexts expose the retained knife/hand relationship without inventing a belt-transfer or release event.",
    "A fresh independent reopening and evaluation of both original and candidate confirms all192 source/candidate bone world matrices, rest matrices, planted-foot bounds, visible prop transforms and action data agree. The redesigned palms retain their evaluated centroids to less than9e-9 world units by this audit. All evaluated candidate topology counts remain invariant.",
    "The candidate is an editable native3D chef with native3D knife and exactly one packed original2D salmon texture. Its packed bytes, plane mesh, UVs and yaw/depth drivers match the original. A reviewer-native work-W frame4 rerender matches the sealed corresponding frame to only1/255 rounding in13 pixels, corroborating native capture provenance."
  ],
  "blockers": [],
  "remainingDifferences": [
    "The target has larger eyes, richer tiny cloth texture/stitching and more pronounced garment hardware. The native candidate uses a quieter matte finish and compact facial detail that remain readable at game size; exact microtexture replication is unnecessary under the frozen criteria.",
    "The lit cap crown is softer and slightly lighter/desaturated blue than the idealized target, while the folded band and underside retain navy depth. This remains within Ellis palette family and supports all-facing readability under one shared light rig.",
    "Rear curl organization and small back garment details are native design choices; the fixed target supplies only a front view. They are coherent and improve the original without pretending an unseen reference exists.",
    "The frozen original salmon remains an explicitly2D display with source facial/body overlap and camera-ray depth bias, especially in side views. It is not physical3D food or evidence of bilateral palm-on-dish contact or a belt release. Its original attachment/visibility behavior is preserved and is accepted as the declared exception."
  ],
